    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Largest crown in the maxillary arch. The crown is relatively short occlusocervically
    but wide mesiodistally and buccolingually (BL slightly greater than MD).



    If
    a Cusp of Carabelli (arrow) is present it is on the lingual of the ML cusp. This
    cusp is the most common example of a tubercle, or elevation on a crown due to
    an extra formation of enamel.



    Contains a central pit within the central
    fossa.



    The primary cusp triangle (trigon) is made up of the ML, MB, and
    DB cusps. The DL cusp is not part of this cusp triangle.



    Cusp size: ML>MB>DB>DL>Carabelli
    (same as 2nd molar)'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
